  <div class="home-prose">
    <p>I’m a data engineer in Mumbai. At ICICI Lombard, I work on ETL pipelines, reporting workflows, and data reconciliation in Oracle. Before that, I worked with Airflow, dbt, and Snowflake at Colgate-Palmolive, and on fraud detection at Card91.</p>
    <p>Outside work, I’m usually building something I want to use. Right now that’s Savory, a searchable home for saved posts, and Pixonomy, a pixel-art game to play with friends. I also run language models locally and build tools around them. More of my <a href="/portfolio/">projects are here</a>, along with my <a href="/resume/">full résumé</a>.</p>
    <p>I write about <a href="/blog/tags/data-engineering/">data pipelines</a>, <a href="/blog/tags/backend/">backend systems</a>, and <a href="/blog/tags/genai/">applied ML</a>. Usually with code, diagrams, and a reason for choosing one approach over another.</p>
    <p>I also love making art, usually in Figma, Blender, or After Effects late at night. Outside that, it’s CS2, Michael Jackson, Elvis, and rock on repeat. Here’s <a href="/now/">what I’m into right now</a> and <a href="/uses/">what’s on my desk</a>.</p>
  </div>
